Annual-report practice links audited statements, notes, strategy, risks, governance, and auditor conclusions.|Investigate why debt-note totals differ from a management presentation.|Best next step?|Reconcile definitions and underlying notes|Choose the smaller number|Average both blindly
Transaction tracing records entries, timing, cash classification, and statement links.|A credit inventory purchase raises inventory and payables without cash.|It immediately increases revenue?|No|Yes|Only if invoiced
Cash-shortage diagnosis reconciles earnings with operating investment, capex, and funding obligations.|Profit ₹20 is outweighed by ₹30 working-capital investment.|The firm can face…?|Cash pressure despite profit|Guaranteed cash surplus|No liquidity risk
Growth creates value when incremental returns justify the capital and risk required.|Incremental ROIC 8% against WACC 12% implies a negative spread.|More identical investment generally…?|Destroys value|Creates value automatically|Eliminates financing needs
Three-statement forecasting links operating drivers, accruals, assets, funding, and checks.|Receivable growth lowers cash conversion in an integrated model.|A balanced model automatically proves realistic assumptions?|No|Yes|Only after formatting
Listed-company valuation triangulates filings, forecasts, claim-consistent models, and market expectations.|DCF and peer values differ because assumptions differ.|Best response?|Explain and test the assumptions|Average mechanically without investigation|Pick the highest
Research writing states thesis, evidence, valuation, catalysts, risks, and falsification conditions.|A report identifies what would invalidate its margin-recovery forecast.|This improves…?|Accountability and decision review|Guaranteed price performance|Only report length
Corporate loan underwriting tests cash repayment, business resilience, structure, collateral, and covenants.|Cash available ₹30 versus debt service ₹20 gives 1.5 coverage.|Collateral alone substitutes for cash analysis?|No|Yes|Only for secured loans
Capex evaluation includes incremental cash, opportunity costs, taxes, timing, risk, and flexibility.|A new machine saves ₹15 annually but requires installation downtime.|Ignoring downtime may…?|Overstate project value|Understate revenue always|Improve precision
Debt-equity comparison weighs costs, dilution, distress, taxes, and funding flexibility.|Debt avoids share issuance but adds scheduled obligations.|Debt is always cheaper economically because its coupon is lower?|No|Yes|Only with tax deductions
Acquisition practice separates target value, synergy, premium, financing, and integration execution.|Synergy PV ₹20 is outweighed by premium ₹25 before costs.|Buyer value is necessarily positive?|No|Yes|Only if EPS rises
Startup fundraising models combine cap tables, option pools, conversion terms, runway, and waterfalls.|A priced round dilutes existing owners and extends cash runway.|Headline valuation alone specifies final ownership?|No|Yes|Only at seed stage
Property evaluation links rents, vacancy, costs, capex, valuation, leverage, and exit assumptions.|Higher interest expense reduces equity cash despite stable property NOI.|Stable NOI guarantees stable equity cash?|No|Yes|Only for offices
Portfolio practice defines goals, exposures, costs, benchmarks, allocation, and review rules.|A portfolio exceeds target equity risk after a rally.|Review should consider…?|Goals and rebalancing rules|Only recent returns|Only winning positions
Stress-testing practice models linked shocks, funding gaps, limits, and feasible responses.|Revenue falls while refinancing becomes unavailable.|Assess…?|Combined cash and solvency consequences|Each shock in isolation only|Only accounting profit
Accounting-failure investigation reconstructs transactions, policies, evidence, control failures, and incentives.|Unsupported sales coincide with unusual related-party balances.|A warning sign alone proves fraud?|No|Yes|Only if profit grows fast
Crisis case studies examine leverage, incentives, liquidity, contagion, and policy responses using dated evidence.|Funding runs force sales that depress collateral values.|The case illustrates…?|Interacting financial feedback|Only one isolated mistake|Guaranteed market efficiency
Thesis review compares forecasts with realised drivers and distinguishes process from luck.|A correct thesis loses money because an unanticipated shock dominates.|Best learning approach?|Record errors, evidence, and process improvements|Judge only the final return|Rewrite the original forecast
